    Fix DST-dependent scheduler conflict test (#8206)
    
    CI tests failed for pull request #8183 on a time-dependent test that
    broke because the run happened just before the US switch from daylight
    saving time back to standard time. In short: Tomorrow at the same time
    is not necessarily 24h away.
    
    SchedulerServiceImplTest.testFindConflictingEvents used the current time
    to schedule events and expected a daily RRule evaluated in
    America/Chicago to hit an event scheduled exactly 24 hours later. The
    RRule keeps the same local time, so whenever a DST change happens within
    the next 24 hours, the second occurrence is shifted by one hour and the
    test fails (e.g. CI runs on 2026-10-31 after 07:00 UTC).
    
    Use a fixed time far away from any DST change instead.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    Basically just read the test, but you can set your clock to right before
    daylight saving time changes and check that the test no longer fails.
    
